packCurrent.sh <hostarch>
    This script packs the content of the out-<hostarch> directory into a .tgz
    file that can be subsequently processed using the updateDXLaprs script.
    The contents of the .tgz archive is in the same form as the pre-built
    images for Linux that can be found at:
        http://dxlaprs.hamspirit.at

    Execute this script at the dxlAPRS/ directory level using the command line:
        ./scripts/packCurrent.sh <hostarch>

    The output will be a file called:
        dxlAPRS_<hostarch>-*.tgz

updateDXLaprs <hostarch> | file [executables]
    If <hostarch> is specified, then dxlAPRS will be installed from a pre-built
    Linux image found on-line at the URL above.

    If a local file is specified instead <hostarch> then this file will be
    used for performing the installation. The local file must be a file that
    was created by the packCurrent.sh script.

    If the "executables" option is specified, then only executable files and
    executable scripts will be updated. All other files in the destination
    directories remain untouched.

Currently, <hostarch> may be:
    armv6tce, armv6, armv7hf, aarch64, x86_32, x86_64
